[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API","page":"API","text":"","title":"API"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#MackeyFunctors.MackeyFunctor","page":"API","text":"MackeyFunctor(G, values, restrictions, transfers, conjugations; coefficient_ring=ZZ)\nMackeyFunctor(coefficient_ring, G, values, restrictions, transfers, conjugations)\n\nA lattice-backed Mackey functor for a finite GAP group G.\n\nThe values dictionary assigns each subgroup a finitely generated abelian group, represented by invariant factors. The restrictions and transfers dictionaries provide matrices for subgroup-lattice cover relations (H, K) with H < K; the constructor closes these maps under composition. The conjugations dictionary provides conjugation maps indexed by (H, g).\n\nAll subgroup keys are canonicalized to the subgroup objects stored in GAP's subgroup lattice, and construction validates the Mackey double-coset formula.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MackeyFunctors.MackeyFunctor"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#MackeyFunctors.MackeyContext","page":"API","text":"MackeyContext(G)\n\nPrecompute subgroup-lattice and double-coset data for a finite GAP group G.\n\nThe field doubleCosetRepresentatives[(j, h, k)] is defined for triples where both subgroups[j] < subgroups[h] and subgroups[k] < subgroups[h] are cover relations. Its value is a vector of representatives for subgroups[j] \\ subgroups[h] / subgroups[k].\n\nEach representative is stored as (word, intersection_index). A word is a vector of (generator_index, exponent) pairs. For example, [(1, 3), (2, -4)] represents generators[1]^3 * generators[2]^-4, and the empty vector represents the identity element. For representative x, intersection_index is the index of subgroups[j]^x intersected with subgroups[k] in subgroups.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MackeyFunctors.MackeyContext"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#MackeyFunctors.double_coset_representative_data","page":"API","text":"double_coset_representative_data(ctx, j, h, k)\ndouble_coset_representative_data(ctx, J, H, K)\n\nReturn representatives for J \\ H / K, where J < H and K < H are cover relations in ctx.\n\nEach representative is returned as (word, intersection_index), where intersection_index points to J^x intersected with K in ctx.subgroups for the represented group element x.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MackeyFunctors.double_coset_representative_data"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#MackeyFunctors.double_coset_representative_words","page":"API","text":"double_coset_representative_words(ctx, j, h, k)\ndouble_coset_representative_words(ctx, J, H, K)\n\nReturn only the generator words from double_coset_representative_data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MackeyFunctors.double_coset_representative_words"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#MackeyFunctors.defines_fg_abelian_map","page":"API","text":"defines_fg_abelian_map(source_group, target_group, M)\n\nReturn true when the integer matrix M defines a homomorphism from the finitely generated abelian group represented by source_group to the one represented by target_group.\n\nGroups are represented by invariant factors: 0 denotes a free Z summand, and a positive integer n denotes a Z/n summand.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MackeyFunctors.defines_fg_abelian_map"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#MackeyFunctors.are_equal_abelian_group_homomorphisms","page":"API","text":"are_equal_abelian_group_homomorphisms(source_group, target_group, M, N)\n\nReturn true when the integer matrices M and N define the same homomorphism between the finitely generated abelian groups represented by source_group and target_group.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MackeyFunctors.are_equal_abelian_group_homomorphisms"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#MackeyFunctors.all_supergroups_from_lattice","page":"API","text":"all_supergroups_from_lattice(G, H)\n\nReturn the proper supergroups K of H in the subgroup lattice of the finite GAP group G.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MackeyFunctors.all_supergroups_from_lattice"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#MackeyFunctors.visualizer_data","page":"API","text":"visualizer_data(M)\n\nReturn a dictionary of subgroup, map, and lattice data for rendering a MackeyFunctor in an external visualizer.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MackeyFunctors.visualizer_data"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#MackeyFunctors.visualizer_json","page":"API","text":"visualizer_json(x)\n\nSerialize visualizer data to the small JSON subset used by the bundled Mackey functor visualizer.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MackeyFunctors.visualizer_json"},{"category":"section","location":"examples/#Examples","page":"Examples","text":"This example constructs the Burnside Mackey functor for the cyclic group C2.\n\nusing GAP\nusing AbstractAlgebra\nusing MackeyFunctors\n\nC2 = GAP.Globals.CyclicGroup(2)\nsubs = Vector{GapObj}(GAP.Globals.AllSubgroups(C2))\ne = subs[1]\ng = GAP.Globals.GeneratorsOfGroup(C2)[1]\n\nvalues = IdDict{GapObj, Vector{Int64}}(\n    e => [0],\n    C2 => [0, 0],\n)\n\nrestrictions = IdDict{Tuple{GapObj, GapObj}, Matrix{Int64}}(\n    (e, C2) => [1 2],\n)\n\ntransfers = IdDict{Tuple{GapObj, GapObj}, Matrix{Int64}}(\n    (e, C2) => [0; 1;;],\n)\n\nconjugations = IdDict{Tuple{GapObj, GapObj}, Matrix{Int64}}(\n    (e, g) => [1;;],\n)\n\nM = MackeyFunctor(C2, values, restrictions, transfers, conjugations)\n\nFor interactive visualization data, use:\n\nvisualizer_data(M)\nvisualizer_json(M)","title":"Examples"},{"category":"section","location":"#MackeyFunctors.jl","page":"Home","text":"MackeyFunctors.jl provides tools for constructing and validating lattice-backed Mackey functor data for finite GAP groups.\n\nThe package represents values as finitely generated abelian groups using invariant factors. A value vector [0, 2, 4] represents Z x Z/2 x Z/4. Restriction, transfer, and conjugation maps are represented by integer matrices between these presentations.","title":"MackeyFunctors.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Home","text":"From the package checkout:\n\nusing Pkg\nPkg.activate(\".\")\nPkg.instantiate()","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Documentation-Build","page":"Home","text":"To build these docs locally:\n\nusing Pkg\nPkg.activate(\"docs\")\nPkg.develop(PackageSpec(path=pwd()))\nPkg.instantiate()\n\nThen run:\n\njulia --project=docs docs/make.jl\n\nThe generated site is written to docs/build/.","title":"Documentation Build"}]
